Upstream license: MIT (see LICENSE)
Upstream author: duoduoler-ops

Modifications for DeepSeek Harness (DSH), 2026:
- Rewrote the skill entry from the Codex `$project-handoff` gesture to the
  DSH `/project-handoff` command and the `skill` tool.
- Removed Codex-specific host instructions (hooks, apply_patch-era tooling,
  list_projects/create_thread/send_message_to_thread/wait_threads/read_thread/
  navigate_to_codex_page, fork_thread/handoff_thread).
- Replaced automatic session continuation with a manual handoff package
  (materials + opening prompt + user-created session), because DSH exposes no
  agent-callable session creation API.
- Removed the compaction counter and Stop-hook final-answer verification from
  the skill text; the reminder logic relies on agent self-assessment.
- Kept the PROJECT_STATE.md structure and BEGIN/END markers unchanged for
  cross-host compatibility.
- Added a DSH-specific README and install instructions.

The companion host plugin `dsh-project-handoff` (a separate repository, not
part of this skill directory) vendors `compaction_reminder.py` as
`python/handoff_state.py`, modified only in how it resolves the SKILL path;
its test suite is adapted from the upstream `tests/` (63 upstream cases kept,
plus 10 DSH event-mapping cases).

This modified version is not endorsed by the upstream author. The upstream
copyright and permission notice are retained as required by the MIT license.
